title: 'Bound get_section_history: it walks every commit and parses the page twice
  per commit'
updated: 2026-11-03T18:20:47Z
---

Found by p5-mcp-hub's k29 research (mounting mcp-wiki in mcp-hub as a shared store). On a 500-page wiki with 1001 commits get_section_history takes 5–8 s; every write is a commit, so a shared wiki hits mcp-hub's 60 s request timeout at roughly 12k commits. Skipping commits where the page's blob is unchanged from the parent took it from 8 s to 0.7 s in a scratch test. Also consider a limit argument.
